#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:2
msgid "What is this?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:4
msgid ""
"Castellum is a subject database system developed at the Max Planck "
"Society."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:7
msgid "Goals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:9
msgid "GDPR compliant data protection and security"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:10
msgid "Flexibility so it can be used in different institutes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:13
msgid "Classification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:15
msgid ""
"You can think of many kinds of scientific databases that handle personal "
"information:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:22
msgid "study database"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:19
msgid "contains all data that is collected during a study"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:21
msgid ""
"only the researchers that are involved with the study have access to the "
"data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:26
msgid "study archive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:25
msgid ""
"contains data from past studies that is relevant for scientific reasons, "
"e.g. reproducibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:34
msgid "research archive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:29
msgid ""
"contains data that has been collected during one study, but may be reused"
" in another one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:32
msgid "reusing data saves time for both the researcher and the test subject"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:34
msgid "examples include image archives and biobanks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:38
msgid "recruting database"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:37
msgid ""
"contains some data about (potential) test subjects that allows you can "
"find out which ones you should contact for your next study"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:47
msgid "contact database"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:41
msgid "a central list of contact information shared by all other databases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:43
msgid ""
"by having this in a central place, contact information can be updated for"
" all studies at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:46
msgid ""
"by having this in a central place, the other databases can work with "
"pseudonyms instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:50
msgid "pseudonym service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:50
msgid "used to store relations between the different datasets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/what.rst:52
msgid ""
"Of these, castellum implements a recruting database, a contact database, "
"and a pseudonym service. All data that is actually related to studies "
"must be stored separately."
msgstr ""

